Installing and building cuda-batch-canny
========================================

Requirements
------------
* An NVIDIA GPU and driver.
* CUDA Toolkit 11.0 or newer (nvcc with C++17 support).
* A C++17 host compiler (GCC 9+ or Clang 10+; for GCC 8 build with
  `make LDLIBS=-lstdc++fs`).
* GNU make and bash.
* Optional: Python 3 with Pillow (montage images and SIPI TIFF conversion),
  wget or curl (SIPI download), clang-format and cpplint (style checks).

No third-party C++ libraries are needed: image I/O and flag parsing are
implemented in src/.

Linux (Ubuntu / Coursera lab)
-----------------------------
    git clone <this repository> cuda-batch-canny
    cd cuda-batch-canny
    make                 # SM is auto-detected via nvidia-smi
    ./run.sh             # generates data, runs every case, writes proof/

If the toolkit is not under /usr/local/cuda:

    make CUDA_PATH=/opt/cuda

To target a specific GPU architecture (e.g. Tesla T4 = 7.5):

    make SM=75

Windows
-------
Use WSL2 with the CUDA-on-WSL driver and follow the Linux steps.
